WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:24.960
I grabbed hold, digging in my claws
te ni totte tsume o tateta

3
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.390
but the future
sono mirai wa

4
00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:34.570
blurred together, colors running
nijimu iro ni kasunde mieta

5
00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:41.210
A red that can swallow even summer's hues
natsu no iro mo nuritsubusu you na aka ni

6
00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:47.930
bokura no koe kakikesareteiku you de
now attempts to blot out our voices

7
00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:54.670
Move those halting feet of yours
tachidomaru sono ashi o fumidasou ze

8
00:00:54.670 --> 00:01:01.310
Don't let stand the lies for show
misekake no uso yarisugosu yori

9
00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:07.560
I'll give up countless mornings for my vows
nandome no asa chikai to hikikaeru yo

10
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:16.110
For the dream that we shared
bokura ga miteita yume

11
00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:35.330
<b>The Ebb and Flow of the Ages</b>

12
00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.800
Punk Hazard
26 years ago

13
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.630
I’m begging you, Vegapunk!

14
00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:42.760
Research the Void Century with me!

15
00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:48.350
This world has a darkness
too deep to ignore!

16
00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:52.230
Conducting this research
requires knowledge from other fields as well.

17
00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:53.810
Please, you’ve got to help me!

18
00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:59.150
As you can plainly see,
I’m a Government scientist now.

19
00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:01.820
I can’t provide you with any data.

20
00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:06.370
How many times have you been caught?
You’re definitely on the Government’s radar!

21
00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:09.120
You understand why
they’re keeping you alive, right?

22
00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:13.040
They’re allowing you to roam free
so that they can root out your associates!

23
00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.250
Pull back now.

24
00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.170
So what of the “darkness”?

25
00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:20.000
One cannot measure
the good and evil of the past!

26
00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.430
A man who bore the name of “D”
was once killed in front of me.

27
00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:30.310
It was out of the blue...

28
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.440
He grew up with me,
been by me since I was born...

29
00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:37.690
He was my older brother.

30
00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:44.360
My true name is Clou D. Clover.

31
00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:47.660
A lie I told in that moment kept me alive.

32
00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.380
H-He’s just my friend!

33
00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.340
No one...

34
00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:13.770
No one in this world should have to die
just for giving out their name!

35
00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:20.400
There are historical records
being erased in secret...

36
00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:27.450
I’m not going to help you,
and I’ll forget you ever told me that.

37
00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.120
Be very careful out there.

38
00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:30.660
Vegapunk!

39
00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.120
I’ll do what I must to find the truth!

40
00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:36.250
The voices of the past will be heard!

41
00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.670
Punk Hazard
22 years ago

42
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.670
You hear about this?!

43
00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:49.340
They say a Buster Call’s being issued
against Ohara in the West Blue!

44
00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:52.680
I wanna witness the slaughter!

45
00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.930
It’s about Clover, the archaeologist!

46
00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:59.650
Looks like the World Government
finally got the goods on him!

47
00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:04.690
No one’s ever gonna try
researching the Void Century ever again!

48
00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:06.650
Now there’s an example,
if I ever saw one!

49
00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:11.740
I’m begging you, Vegapunk!

50
00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:18.710
Seems one Oharan kid
got away from the Buster Call!

51
00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:19.370
Huh?!

52
00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:22.590
They put a child this young
on the wanted list?

53
00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:43.690
Surely you had time to escape...

54
00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:50.660
Clover!

55
00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:58.620
Did you all die just to preserve
this vast store of texts for the future?!

56
00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:03.000
The absurdity of it all!

57
00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.130
How crazy would you have to be,

58
00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:09.880
daring to risk certain death
to continue your research?!

59
00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:23.440
Someone once told me that
 the voices of the past would be heard...

60
00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:27.860
History is written by the victors.

61
00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:35.660
The voices of the vanquished,
sunk deep beneath the sea, are barely audible.

62
00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:41.540
But the truth, discovered
through great sacrifice...

63
00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:44.580
has now been conveyed to the world.

64
00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:51.010
I pray that this broadcast, up to this point,
 has safely reached the ears of everyone.

65
00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:57.430
Hey, what the hell’re we waitin’ for?!
Blast off already!

66
00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:59.140
No, we can’t do that!

67
00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:02.350
That horse-gramps is gonna attack us again!

68
00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:04.850
And that’s exactly why we can’t leave!

69
00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:10.900
I understand that this ship is equipped
with a booster capable of launching us one kilometer.

70
00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:16.370
But if that monster slows down
our approach velocity even a bit,

71
00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:20.120
we’ll be thrown off trajectory!

72
00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:24.210
The wind’s blowing to the north!
A tailwind would reduce our lift,

73
00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:27.670
and in my estimate,
the ship wouldn’t reach the water,

74
00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:30.380
but crash into the ground instead!

75
00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:34.090
In other words,
unless we get rid of that old geezer...

76
00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.220
Whuh?!

77
00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:40.140
Huh?!

78
00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:41.060
Wha?!

79
00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:43.230
Atlas?!

80
00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:57.110
A giant boar, snake, bird, and robot?!

81
00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:59.830
What’s going on, Vice Admiral Hound?!

82
00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:02.660
Don’t know... I didn’t hear about any of this!

83
00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:11.420
The giant Robo!

84
00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:13.920
Is that an iron Giant?!

85
00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:16.630
Joyboy...

86
00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:20.350
I’m so happy... I get to see you again!

87
00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:25.350
I’m talking to you!

88
00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.440
Who’re you even talking about?

89
00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:33.610
You go ahead.

90
00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:39.910
Your enemy is my enemy.

91
00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:42.490
Oh, I’m so happy...

92
00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:45.580
I get to fight for you again...

93
00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:48.420
Joyboy!

94
00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:51.630
Amazing! You can talk!

95
00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:54.590
Unless we crush it into tiny pieces...

96
00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:58.340
Vegapunk’s speech will not end,
so it would seem.

97
00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:02.300
Joyboy is in danger...

98
00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:06.430
I must protect him!

99
00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:09.230
Alright, guys!

100
00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:10.520
Get this ship moving!

101
00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:17.240
Hey! Is that thing on our side, Straw Hat?

102
00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:19.740
Uhh, I dunno...

103
00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:23.490
but he’s been saying
he’s gonna protect this Joyboy guy.

104
00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:24.700
Who’s that?

105
00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:26.330
“Saying”?!

106
00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:28.330
I haven’t heard a thing!

107
00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:30.170
Huh? Really?

108
00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:33.630
Don’t just let them get away!
Maintain fire!

109
00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:41.640
It would be foolish to hear the account of a war
that happened 900 years ago from only one side.

110
00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:46.220
History must be approached
 from multiple perspectives.

111
00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:48.930
I wish I had more time.

112
00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:50.310
But...

113
00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:53.980
there are forces in motion
 who can no longer be stopped!

114
00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:17.760
It’s winding up!
It’s gonna shoot something!

115
00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:28.850
Huh?

116
00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:30.430
Whaaa?!

117
00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:32.600
Watch out, Robo!

118
00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:41.860
Aaahhh! Robo!

119
00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:45.620
It’s a 900-year-old weapon!
Of course it didn’t work!

120
00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:48.330
Peter! Crush it between your jaws!

121
00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:50.540
Stop the broadcast!

122
00:09:57.250 --> 00:09:59.420
There is no escaping me,

123
00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:02.630
Kuma, Bonney!

124
00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:08.350
Are you okay, Lilith?!

125
00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:11.430
W-Why’d you do that to Lilith?!

126
00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:21.360
Take care of Lilith!

127
00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:22.240
Huh?

128
00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:22.860
What?

129
00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:25.530
What? Atlas?

130
00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:31.040
Get airborne! I’ll take out
anything in your way!

131
00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.290
What do you mean?!

132
00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:40.460
Lilith’s access is cut off!
Only Atlas is left!

133
00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:44.880
C’mon, Atlas!
Talk to us, what gives?!

134
00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:46.050
Hey!

135
00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:54.060
Zoro! Get Lilith inside!

136
00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:55.020
On it!

137
00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:57.600
Jinbe?!

138
00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:58.650
Let’s go!

139
00:10:58.650 --> 00:11:01.610
If we don’t act fast,
we’re going to regret it!

140
00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:03.190
Brook! Do it!

141
00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:05.320
As you wish, Zoro!

142
00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:12.950
Coup de...

143
00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:32.260
Burst!

144
00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:50.240
The Sunny!

145
00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:52.160
Hang on tight! Going down!

146
00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:53.200
No!

147
00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:55.660
Wait a second!

148
00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:58.830
Are we even going to make it?!

149
00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:05.920
You would sacrifice yourself...?

150
00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:20.730
Nope... This service’s on the house.

151
00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:27.400
Atlas!

152
00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:30.360
Huh?!

153
00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:35.200
We’re gonna make it...

154
00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:37.500
all the way to the water!

155
00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:40.750
No, you can’t do that to us, Atlas!

156
00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:43.920
It’s not right!

157
00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.630
Atlas is gone!

158
00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:52.840
I’s the only Vegapunk in the world now!

159
00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:59.020
No, not yet...

160
00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:01.980
Not while Stella continues to babble on!

161
00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:07.940
25 years ago,

162
00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:13.950
the pirate Gol D. Roger at last completed
 the world’s first circumnavigation.

163
00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:19.200
And he and his crew
 surely must have heard...

164
00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:21.830
the purest voice of the past.

165
00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:23.080
Wh-What?

166
00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:25.540
What does he mean, “Gol D.”?

167
00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:27.880
So,

168
00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:30.760
I think everyone has realized by now,

169
00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:34.510
but this is my projection for the future.

170
00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:50.280
We will stop it at once!

171
00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:52.110
Of course we will.

172
00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:56.620
Oh no, no, no...

173
00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:58.990
I’m all rusty now...

174
00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:03.710
This is the right time, isn’t it?

175
00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:06.210
Joyboy...

176
00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:09.840
I’m gonna use it.

177
00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:12.840
Fire!

178
00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:14.970
Don’t let them get away!

179
00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:26.610
Don't touch the claws! They're venomous!

180
00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:31.530
It’s not like we want to...!

181
00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:33.780
But he’s not letting up!

182
00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:37.240
He just keeps comin’,
down to the very end!

183
00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:49.500
Saturn!

184
00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:54.340
If there’s one score I gotta settle...

185
00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:56.340
It’s with you!

186
00:14:59.350 --> 00:15:01.930
Distortion Future!

187
00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:10.020
Pirate whelp!

188
00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:12.150
You shall be first to perish!

189
00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:16.320
You dare...!

190
00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:33.550
Future Where...

191
00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:41.850
I’m the Most Free!

192
00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:47.020
Bonney?!

193
00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:48.980
St. Saturn!

194
00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:52.020
I’ll deal with you!

195
00:15:52.020 --> 00:15:55.400
That’s it, Bonney! You do it!

196
00:15:57.400 --> 00:16:02.200
One day, the memories of
the Void Century will surface!

197
00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:09.670
In fact, the weapons that sank
all the continents in a man-made disaster...

198
00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:12.840
still exist today, by someone’s design.

199
00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:19.260
The machinations of history and fate
 seem to insist upon the obliteration of...

200
00:16:19.260 --> 00:16:21.930
those last descendants
 of rare races!

201
00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:25.640
Are you by chance a Buccaneer?!

202
00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:28.350
What makes my blood so different
from other people?

203
00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:35.480
I hear there was a “Land of the Gods”
atop the Red Line, long ago.

204
00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:37.610
You’re a Lunarian, aren’t ya?

205
00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:41.490
The Government’ll give you
a hundred million berries for info!

206
00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:43.580
I gotta say, you’re creepy!

207
00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.910
Look, she’s got three eyes!

208
00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:51.080
It’s Nika!

209
00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:57.170
What a pale imitation!

210
00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:16.020
Saturn!

211
00:17:17.730 --> 00:17:19.190
Ha, jerk!

212
00:17:19.190 --> 00:17:21.360
Follow the Nikas!

213
00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:32.250
How dare you do that to my dad?!

214
00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:37.590
Your only options
are slavery and death.

215
00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:40.470
Such is history’s decree.

216
00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:44.720
How dare you do that to my mom?!

217
00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:49.810
It was also I who conducted
drug experiments on your mother.

218
00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:53.350
There’s no way that you guys are gods...

219
00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:00.990
But gods do exist!

220
00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:04.450
Bonney. It’s me, your mommy!

221
00:18:05.820 --> 00:18:07.870
He’ll show up and save you!

222
00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:13.000
And heroes are real, too!

223
00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:19.550
I wish the three of us
could have lived together!

224
00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:23.420
So many times I’ve thought
I’d rather die than be alone!

225
00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:26.430
But no... I’m gonna live!

226
00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:28.430
Because my parents...

227
00:18:30.680 --> 00:18:33.180
wanted me to be happy!

228
00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:46.950
There, there. Good girl!

229
00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:52.370
Hey, Kumachi...

230
00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:54.580
I’m so happy.

231
00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:56.460
As am I.

232
00:18:58.380 --> 00:18:59.710
Bonney...

233
00:19:06.380 --> 00:19:08.430
Thank you...

234
00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:09.600
for being born!

235
00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:28.030
Damned insects, all of you!

236
00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:30.280
Begone!

237
00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:35.000
Liberation...

238
00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:43.750
Nika Punch!

239
00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:16.330
Should anything happen,

240
00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:20.920
it is my sincere wish that
 you all keep yourselves safe.

241
00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:26.590
No matter what happens,

242
00:20:26.590 --> 00:20:30.590
I believe in human wisdom!

243
00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:33.350
I believe in science!

244
00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:41.520
It’s been 25 years
 since Roger died.

245
00:20:42.230 --> 00:20:44.730
It’s been two years
 since Whitebeard died.

246
00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:49.950
But the fall of these legends
was merely the prologue of a new era!

247
00:20:51.070 --> 00:20:51.950
As such...

248
00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:56.740
those who refuse to buckle under
any and all suppression...

249
00:20:57.870 --> 00:20:59.750
might indeed, quite ironically...

250
00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:04.210
be the ones closest of all
 to reaching the truth!

251
00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:14.850
Sent ‘im flyin’!

252
00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:17.220
Hey, Bonney!

253
00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:19.230
Ya did good!

254
00:21:30.110 --> 00:21:31.570
Look!

255
00:21:31.570 --> 00:21:33.320
That’s your ship, right?!

256
00:21:33.740 --> 00:21:35.280
The Sunny!

257
00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:38.660
Falling—dying—help—
falling—dying—help!

258
